#: .landing.hero.eyebrow
msgid "Arch Linux · Configuration as data · {{release}}"
msgstr "Arch Linux · Configuraziun sco datas · {{release}}"

#: .landing.hero.title
msgid "An installer that <em>knows what it’s doing.</em>"
msgstr "In installatur che <em>sa tge ch’el fa.</em>"

#: .landing.hero.lede
msgid "Vanilla Arch underneath. A configuration knowledge base on top — every setting, every interaction between settings, transparently encoded."
msgstr "Sutvart in Arch nunmidà. Survart ina basa da savida da la configuraziun – mintga parameter, mintga interacziun tranter ils parameters, tut codifitgà en moda transparenta."

#: .landing.cta.download
msgid "Download ISO"
msgstr "Telechargiar l’ISO"

#: .landing.cta.source
msgid "Source on GitHub"
msgstr "Code da funtauna sin GitHub"

#: .landing.principles.eyebrow
msgid "What makes it different"
msgstr "Tge che fa la differenza"

#: .landing.principles.title
msgid "Three principles, applied throughout."
msgstr "Trais princips, applitgads consequentamain."

#: .landing.principles.transparent.num
msgid "01 — TRANSPARENT"
msgstr "01 – TRANSPARENT"

#: .landing.principles.transparent.title
msgid "Every choice is data"
msgstr "Tut las tschernas èn datas"

#: .landing.principles.transparent.body
msgid "Settings, dependencies, and lifecycle scripts live in a KDL knowledge base — auditable, forkable, fetched at install time so improvements ship without re-spinning an ISO."
msgstr "Parameters, dependenzas e scripts dal ciclus da vita sa chattan en ina basa da savida KDL – controllabla, disponibla per in fork, telechargiada durant l’installaziun, uschia che meglieraziuns vegnan furnidas senza crear in nov ISO."

#: .landing.principles.hardened.num
msgid "02 — HARDENED"
msgstr "02 – RINFORZÀ"

#: .landing.principles.hardened.title
msgid "Security by default"
msgstr "Segirezza sco standard"

#: .landing.principles.hardened.body
msgid "Per-CPU vulnerability mitigation, system hardening sysctls, restricted user namespaces, optional hardened_malloc. Opt-out, not opt-in — and every trade-off is explained where you make it."
msgstr "Mitigiaziun da mancanzas da segirezza adattada a mintga CPU, sysctls per il rinforzament dal sistem, spazis da num da l’utilisader restrenschids, hardened_malloc opziunal. Activà sco standard, betg mo sin dumonda – e mintga cumpromiss vegn declerà là nua che Vus decidais."

#: .landing.principles.desktops.num
msgid "03 — FOUR DESKTOPS"
msgstr "03 – QUATTER DESKTOPS"

#: .landing.principles.desktops.title
msgid "XFCE · Wayfire · Niri · COSMIC"
msgstr "XFCE · Wayfire · Niri · COSMIC"

#: .landing.principles.desktops.body
msgid "Pick one, or install all four side by side and switch from the greeter. Wayfire and Niri come with waybar, nwg-launchers and nwgbar already configured; XFCE and COSMIC bring their own panels. None of them is a stripped-down minimum."
msgstr "Tscherni in desktop, u installai tuts quatter in sper l’auter e midai tranter els en il greeter. Wayfire e Niri èn equipads cun waybar, nwg-launchers e nwgbar gia configurads; XFCE e COSMIC portan lur agens panels. Nagin dad els n’è reducì al minimum."

#: .landing.desktops.eyebrow
msgid "Choose, mix, switch"
msgstr "Tscherner, cumbinar, midar"

#: .landing.desktops.title
msgid "Four equal desktops, not one default and three afterthoughts."
msgstr "Quatter desktops equivalents, betg in desktop da standard e trais agiuntas secundaras."

#: .landing.desktops.lede
msgid "Wayfire and Niri are commonly considered incomplete environments. Ditana ships everything they need — a polished waybar, nwg-launcher, nwgbar, and a consistent panel layout — and treats all four desktops as first-class citizens."
msgstr "Wayfire e Niri vegnan per il solit considerads sco ambients incumplets. Ditana furnescha tut quai ch’els dovran – in waybar bain elavurà, nwg-launcher, nwgbar ed ina disposiziun coerenta dals panels – e tracta tut ils quatter desktops sco opziuns da plaina valur."

#: .landing.desktops.xfce.alt
msgid "XFCE on Ditana with Blue Flat theme, Firefox, Thunar"
msgstr "XFCE sin Ditana cun il tema Blue Flat, Firefox, Thunar"

#: .landing.desktops.xfce.caption
msgid "<strong>XFCE</strong> — Xorg, mature, fast"
msgstr "<strong>XFCE</strong> – Xorg, madir, svelt"

#: .landing.desktops.wayfire.alt
msgid "Wayfire on Ditana with Blue Vibrant theme, Brave, Thunar"
msgstr "Wayfire sin Ditana cun il tema Blue Vibrant, Brave, Thunar"

#: .landing.desktops.wayfire.caption
msgid "<strong>Wayfire</strong> — Wayland, Compiz-inspired"
msgstr "<strong>Wayfire</strong> – Wayland, inspirà da Compiz"

#: .landing.desktops.niri.alt
msgid "Niri on Ditana with Blue Vibrant theme, Brave, COSMIC Files"
msgstr "Niri sin Ditana cun il tema Blue Vibrant, Brave, COSMIC Files"

#: .landing.desktops.niri.caption
msgid "<strong>Niri</strong> — Wayland, scrollable tiling"
msgstr "<strong>Niri</strong> – Wayland, tiling cun scrollar"

#: .landing.desktops.cosmic.alt
msgid "COSMIC on Ditana with Amber Rounded theme, LibreWolf, Thunar"
msgstr "COSMIC sin Ditana cun il tema Amber Rounded, LibreWolf, Thunar"

#: .landing.desktops.cosmic.caption
msgid "<strong>COSMIC</strong> — Wayland, System76’s Rust desktop"
msgstr "<strong>COSMIC</strong> – Wayland, il desktop da System76 en Rust"

#: .landing.snapshots.eyebrow
msgid "Rolling release, without the risk"
msgstr "Rolling release, senza il ristg"

#: .landing.snapshots.title
msgid "Every upgrade is reversible."
msgstr "Mintga actualisaziun è reversibla."

#: .landing.snapshots.lede
msgid "Arch’s rolling-release model is a feature, not a bug — but it can land breakage on a Tuesday morning. Ditana takes the sting out by snapshotting the system before every upgrade, automatically."
msgstr "Il model da rolling release dad Arch è ina funcziunalitad, betg in’errur – ma el po donnegiar insatge in mardi damaun. Ditana mitigescha quest privel cun far automaticamain in snapshot dal sistem avant mintga actualisaziun."

#: .landing.snapshots.subtitle
msgid "Atomic snapshots, taken by a pacman hook."
msgstr "Snapshots atomars, fatgs d’in hook da pacman."

#: .landing.snapshots.alt
msgid "System maintenance dialog showing automatic system snapshots option enabled by default"
msgstr "Dialog dal mantegniment dal sistem cun l’opziun dals snapshots automatics dal sistem, activada sco standard"

#: .landing.snapshots.p1
msgid "On ZFS and BTRFS, snapshots are atomic and free — a few milliseconds before any package upgrade. On XFS and EXT4, Timeshift handles the same job via rsync, completing typical incremental snapshots in seconds."
msgstr "Sin ZFS e BTRFS èn ils snapshots atomars e senza custs – in pèr millisecundas avant mintga actualisaziun da pachets. Sin XFS ed EXT4 fa Timeshift la medema lavur cun rsync e terminescha en paucas secundas ils snapshots tipics, che cuntegnan mo las midadas."

#: .landing.snapshots.p2
msgid "The first snapshot is created by the installer itself, just before the first reboot. That means you can roll back to a freshly-installed system from day one — no setup, no first-upgrade chicken-and-egg."
msgstr "L’emprim snapshot vegn creà da l’installatur sez, curt avant l’emprim reaviar. Quai munta che Vus pudais restaurar in sistem gist installà a partir da l’emprim di – nagina configuraziun, nagin problem da la giaglina e da l’ov cun l’emprima actualisaziun."

#: .landing.snapshots.p3
msgid "System snapshots, not data snapshots: <code>/home</code> and other data volumes are never touched. Roll back the system; keep your work."
msgstr "Snapshots dal sistem, betg snapshots da datas: <code>/home</code> ed auters volumens da datas na vegnan mai tutgads. Restaurai il sistem, mantegnai Vossa lavur."

#: .landing.snapshots.p4
msgid "For ZFS, Ditana ships its own <a href=\"https://github.com/acrion/zfs-autosnap\">zfs-autosnap</a> fork that — unlike the upstream — removes the pacman lock file from the snapshot, so a rollback leaves you with a working pacman immediately."
msgstr "Per ZFS furnescha Ditana ses agen fork da <a href=\"https://github.com/acrion/zfs-autosnap\">zfs-autosnap</a> che – al cuntrari dal project d’origin – allontanescha la datoteca da bloccada da pacman dal snapshot, uschia ch’in pacman che funcziuna è disponibel immediatamain suenter ina restauraziun."

#: .landing.headless.title
msgid "Headless too."
msgstr "Er senza interfatscha grafica."

#: .landing.headless.body
msgid "System hardening plus automatic snapshots make Ditana a viable Arch-based server choice — uncommon for a rolling release. The installer’s <em>Server</em> profile skips the desktop install entirely and leans into the security defaults."
msgstr "Il rinforzament dal sistem ed ils snapshots automatics fan da Ditana ina tscherna raschunaivla per in server sin basa dad Arch – nunusità per in rolling release. Il profil <em>Server</em> da l’installatur sursiglia cumplettamain l’installaziun dal desktop e metta l’accent sin las valurs da standard da segirezza."

#: .landing.hardware.eyebrow
msgid "Hardware-aware"
msgstr "Adattà a la hardware"

#: .landing.hardware.title
msgid "It checks the upstream sources at install time."
msgstr "Durant l’installaziun vegnan controlladas las funtaunas d’origin."

#: .landing.hardware.nvidia.alt
msgid "NVIDIA driver decision dialog with detected PCI ID and recommendation rationale"
msgstr "Dialog da decisiun per il driver NVIDIA cun l’ID PCI identifitgà e la motivaziun da la recumandaziun"

#: .landing.hardware.nvidia.title
msgid "NVIDIA detection, four-way decision."
msgstr "Identificaziun NVIDIA, decisiun tranter quatter variantas."

#: .landing.hardware.nvidia.p1
msgid "Ditana queries the live PCI ID lists from <code>github.com/NVIDIA/open-gpu-kernel-modules</code> and the official legacy GPU page at install time. Based on the result, it recommends one of four driver options – nvidia-open-dkms, the legacy proprietary <code>nvidia-580xx-dkms</code>, the older <code>nvidia-470xx-dkms</code>, or nouveau – and checks that the package it is about to recommend is present in the repository, reverting to nouveau when it is not."
msgstr "Durant l’installaziun consultescha Ditana las glistas actualas dals IDs PCI da <code>github.com/NVIDIA/open-gpu-kernel-modules</code> e la pagina uffiziala da las GPUs pli veglias. Sin basa dal resultat recumonda Ditana ina da quatter opziuns da driver – nvidia-open-dkms, il driver proprietar per GPUs pli veglias <code>nvidia-580xx-dkms</code>, il driver anc pli vegl <code>nvidia-470xx-dkms</code> u nouveau – e controllescha ch’il pachet che Ditana vul recumandar è disponibel en il repositori; sch’el manca, recumonda Ditana nouveau."

#: .landing.hardware.nvidia.p2
msgid "It then explains what it picked, and why."
msgstr "Lura vegn declerà tge che Ditana ha tschernì e pertge."

#: .landing.cpu.title
msgid "CPU vulnerabilities, detected and mitigated."
msgstr "Mancanzas da segirezza da la CPU, identifitgadas e mitigiadas."

#: .landing.cpu.p1
msgid "Spectre v2, Meltdown, MDS, TAA, MMIO Stale Data, RETBleed, SRSO, GDS, RFDS — Ditana reads <code>/sys/devices/system/cpu/vulnerabilities/</code> at install time, <a href=\"/under-the-hood/mitigations/\">enables only the mitigations your CPU actually needs</a>, and lets you review each one with documentation."
msgstr "Spectre v2, Meltdown, MDS, TAA, MMIO Stale Data, RETBleed, SRSO, GDS, RFDS – durant l’installaziun legia Ditana <code>/sys/devices/system/cpu/vulnerabilities/</code>, <a href=\"/under-the-hood/mitigations/\">activescha mo las mitigiaziuns che Vossa CPU dovra effectivamain</a> ed As lascha examinar mintgina cun la documentaziun correspundenta."

#: .landing.cpu.p2
msgid "Every mitigation comes with its <em>cost</em> spelled out, so you can make an informed call instead of choosing between “secure default” and “fast default” blindly."
msgstr "Per mintga mitigiaziun vegn ses <em>cust</em> numnà explicitamain, uschia che Vus pudais prender ina decisiun fundada, empè da tscherner a l’orva tranter «standard segir» e «standard svelt»."

#: .landing.cpu.alt
msgid "CPU vulnerability mitigation dialog showing detected vulnerabilities and selectable mitigations"
msgstr "Dialog da las mitigiaziuns da mancanzas da segirezza da la CPU cun las mancanzas da segirezza identifitgadas e las mitigiaziuns che Vus pudais tscherner"

#: .landing.hardening.alt
msgid "System hardening options dialog"
msgstr "Dialog cun las opziuns dal rinforzament dal sistem"

#: .landing.hardening.title
msgid "System hardening, opt-out by default."
msgstr "Rinforzament dal sistem, activà sco standard."

#: .landing.hardening.body
msgid "Unprivileged user namespaces restricted to the programs that need them. Restricted ptrace. Hidden kernel pointers. Hardened FIFO and regular-file protection in sticky directories. SYN cookies, no ICMP redirects, no source routing, reverse-path filtering. Each option ships enabled, each one is explained – and developers get a profile that loosens the right things for debugging."
msgstr "Spazis da num da l’utilisader senza privilegis, restrenschids als programs che als dovran. Restricziun da ptrace. Punctaders dal kernel zuppads. Protecziun rinforzada per FIFOs e datotecas regularas en ordinaturs sticky. SYN cookies, nagins ICMP redirects, nagin source routing, filtraziun reverse-path. Mintga opziun vegn furnida activada, mintgina vegn declerada – e per il svilup da software datti in profil che schlucca precis las dretgas restricziuns per debugar."

#: .landing.installer.eyebrow
msgid "The installer itself"
msgstr "L’installatur sez"

#: .landing.installer.title
msgid "Ten categories. Sensible defaults. No mystery."
msgstr "Diesch categorias. Valurs da standard raschunaivlas. Nagins misteris."

#: .landing.installer.lede
msgid "Tell the installer who you are – originating from a different distribution, migrating from KDE Plasma, Cinnamon, Xfce or MATE, working as a developer, running as a server, or falling into none of these – and it accordingly pre-flips checkboxes. You may examine and revise every single one prior to the start of installation."
msgstr "Communitgai a l’installatur tgi che Vus essas – sche Vus vegnis d’ina autra distribuziun, midais da KDE Plasma, Cinnamon, Xfce u MATE, sviluppais software, utilisais il sistem sco server u sche nagin da quai na correspunda – ed el mida ordavant il stadi da las chaschettas da controlla correspundentas. Vus pudais examinar e modifitgar mintgina avant il cumenzament da l’installaziun."

#: .landing.installer.categories.alt
msgid "Configuration categories overview dialog"
msgstr "Dialog cun la survista da las categorias da configuraziun"

#: .landing.installer.categories.title
msgid "One screen, the whole system."
msgstr "In visur, l’entir sistem."

#: .landing.installer.categories.body
msgid "Configuration categories let you drill into desktops, browsers, file managers, office suites, AI tools, terminals, kernels, filesystems, hardening, mitigations, and the system allocator — all from one menu, all reversible, all explained."
msgstr "Las categorias da configuraziun As permettan d’examinar en detagl desktops, navigaturs, gestiunaris da datotecas, programs da biro, utensils d’IA, terminals, kernels, sistems da datotecas, rinforzament, mitigiaziuns e l’allocator dal sistem – tut or d’in unic menu, tut reversibel, tut declerà."

#: .landing.installer.impact.title
msgid "Every change comes with its impact."
msgstr "Per mintga midada vegnan mussads ses effects."

#: .landing.installer.impact.body
msgid "Toggle an option, see the consequence: which packages get added, which scripts will run, what other settings flip in response. The settings graph is data — Ditana shows you the path through it."
msgstr "Midai in’opziun e guardai la consequenza: tge pachets che vegnan agiuntads, tge scripts che vegnan exequids, tge auters parameters che sa midan en reacziun. Il graf dals parameters consista da datas – Ditana As mussa la via tras el."

#: .landing.installer.impact.alt
msgid "Settings impact overview showing dependent changes"
msgstr "Survista dals effects dals parameters cun las midadas dependentas"

#: .landing.config.eyebrow
msgctxt ".landing.config.eyebrow"
msgid "Configuration as data"
msgstr "Configuraziun sco datas"

#: .landing.config.title
msgid "The installer is small. The knowledge base is big."
msgstr "L’installatur è pitschen. La basa da savida è gronda."

#: .landing.config.lede
msgid "A Linux installer should do more than partition, install packages, and hand off. PKGBUILDs only know about their own package — they can’t know what else is on the system. Ditana keeps the cross-cutting decisions in a separate, auditable knowledge base."
msgstr "In installatur da Linux duess far dapli che crear partiziuns, installar pachets e surdar il sistem. Ils PKGBUILDs enconuschan mo lur agen pachet – els na pon betg savair tge ch’è anc sin il sistem. Ditana tegna las decisiuns che pertutgan plirs pachets en ina basa da savida separada e controllabla."

#: .landing.config.kdl.title
msgid "Settings declare their dependencies in plain KDL."
msgstr "Ils parameters decleran lur dependenzas en KDL simpel."

#: .landing.config.kdl.body
msgid "This excerpt says: install kitty <em>only</em> if the chosen terminal operates on Wayland alone <em>and</em> XFCE is also installed. Nobody would consider requesting that, and nobody needs to: the rule stands beside the package list, where a reviewer can see both the condition and the reason for it, rather than being hidden within installer code."
msgstr "Quest extract di: installar kitty <em>mo</em> sch’il terminal tschernì funcziuna exclusivamain sin Wayland <em>e</em> sche XFCE è er installà. Nagina persuna na pensass da dumandar quai, e quai n’è er betg necessari: la regla stat sper la glista dals pachets, nua ch’ina persuna che examinescha vesa tant la cundiziun sco er il motiv per ella, empè d’esser zuppada en il code da l’installatur."

#: .landing.config.browse
msgid "Browse ditana-config →"
msgstr "Explorar ditana-config →"

#: .landing.final.title
msgid "Ready to try it?"
msgstr "Vulais Vus empruvar Ditana?"

#: .landing.final.body
msgid "Ditana {{release}} is a {{size}} ISO with a detached GPG signature. It fetches its packages and its configuration while it installs, so a working network connection is part of the requirements. The full install takes 15–45 minutes depending on what you pick."
msgstr "Ditana {{release}} è in ISO da {{size}} cun ina signatura GPG separada. Durant l’installaziun telechargia el ses pachets e sia configuraziun; perquai fa ina connexiun a la rait che funcziuna part da las premissas. L’installaziun cumpletta dura 15 – 45 minutas, tenor quai che Vus tschernis."

#: .landing.final.whatsNew
msgid "What’s new in {{release}}"
msgstr "Novitads da la versiun {{release}}"
